{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1492259-assassins-missing-conditions","id":1492259,"title":"Assassins' missing conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-09-03T19:25:27-07:00","id":1492259,"title":"Assassins' missing conditions","content":"In the Assassins book it mentions several conditions with no explanation in the book for them, Doomed, Painted Target, Sudden Peril. Can one of the developers let us know what these do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-03T21:09:11-07:00","id":1492262,"title":"","content":"Nevermind, I discovered what those three conditions do. Their explanations are buried in the text.<br /> <br /> <b>Doomed:</b> The Injury and Critical stunts have their cost reduced by the points of the Doomed Condition on a target, to a minimum of 1. The Doomed Condition resolves at the end of a scene or when the Assassin is no longer pursuing the Doomed individual, whichever happens last.<br /> <br /> <b>Painted Target:</b> You gain an Enhancement bonus equal to their points in the Painted Target Condition to any rolls related to tracking them down or reaching a target. Once you reach your target, resolve this Condition.<br /> <br /> <b>Sudden Peril:</b> The target gains a Complication equal to the points they have in the Sudden Peril Condition. For every point the target doesn\u2019t resolve when taking actions during the scene, they suffer 1 Injury Condition or Health Box. You may make this contingent on an action the target takes (such as \u201cgetting on the bus\u201d or \u201centering the conference room\u201d), which then requires a successful Procedural Investigation roll to determine your involvement. Sudden Peril resolves after it\u2019s been triggered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}